@startuml
title III-07 - Customer shopping cart, ordering and VNPay Sandbox payment

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Customer
boundary "Customer Portal" as Web
control "Order API" as API
database "CRM Database" as DB
participant "VNPay Sandbox" as VNP
participant "Payment Timeout Scheduler" as Job

== Cart management ==

Customer -> Web: Add, edit or remove cart item
Web -> API: PUT /api/cart
API -> DB: Save cart changes
DB --> API: Cart saved
API --> Web: Cart summary
Web --> Customer: Show updated cart

== Create order and reserve stock ==

Customer -> Web: Confirm address and payment method
Web -> API: POST /api/orders\n(cart, address, paymentMethod)
API -> DB: BEGIN transaction
API -> DB: Lock products and read current stock

alt Insufficient stock or invalid item
    API -> DB: ROLLBACK
    API --> Web: 409 OUT_OF_STOCK / 400 INVALID_CART
    Web --> Customer: Show checkout error
else Stock available
    API -> DB: Insert order (PENDING_PAYMENT)
    API -> DB: Insert order_items
    API -> DB: Reserve/decrease stock
    API -> DB: COMMIT transaction
    API -> API: Create unique vnp_TxnRef
    API -> API: Build signed VNPay payment URL
    API --> Web: 201 paymentUrl
    Web -> VNP: Redirect to paymentUrl
    Customer -> VNP: Complete payment in Sandbox

    == Return URL: display only ==

    VNP --> Web: Redirect to Return URL with vnp_* params
    Web -> API: GET /api/payments/vnpay/return
    API -> API: Verify vnp_SecureHash
    alt Invalid Return URL checksum
        API --> Web: Invalid payment result
        Web --> Customer: Show verification error
    else Valid Return URL checksum
        API --> Web: Show payment result
        Web --> Customer: Show result
        note right of Web
          Return URL is for customer display.
          It does not finalize the order.
        end note
    end

    == IPN: server-to-server source of truth ==

    VNP ->> API: GET /api/payments/vnpay/ipn\n(vnp_* params)
    API -> API: Verify checksum, vnp_TxnRef,\namount and transaction status

    alt Invalid signature or mismatched transaction
        API --> VNP: HTTP 200 {RspCode:97, Message:Invalid data}
    else Valid callback
        API -> DB: BEGIN payment update transaction
        API -> DB: SELECT payment/order FOR UPDATE
        API -> DB: Insert IPN event\nUNIQUE(order_id, ipn_type)

        alt Success: responseCode=00 and transactionStatus=00
            API -> DB: Update payment PAID
            API -> DB: Update order CONFIRMED
            API -> DB: COMMIT
            API --> VNP: HTTP 200 {RspCode:00, Message:Confirm Success}
        else Failed or expired payment
            API -> DB: Update payment FAILED/CANCELLED
            API -> DB: Release reserved stock once
            API -> DB: COMMIT
            API --> VNP: HTTP 200 {RspCode:00, Message:Confirm Success}
        else Duplicate IPN callback
            API -> DB: No-op because state is already final
            API -> DB: COMMIT
            API --> VNP: HTTP 200 {RspCode:02, Message:Order already confirmed}
        end
    end
end

== Expired pending-payment cleanup ==

Job -> API: Run every 5 minutes
API -> DB: BEGIN cleanup transaction
API -> DB: SELECT PENDING_PAYMENT orders older than timeout\nFOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
alt Expired orders found
    API -> DB: Update payment EXPIRED
    API -> DB: Update order CANCELLED
    API -> DB: Release reserved stock once
    API -> DB: COMMIT
else No expired orders
    API -> DB: COMMIT
end

note over API,DB
  Payment secrets stay on the backend.
  IPN handling must be idempotent: a retry cannot confirm twice,
  create a duplicate payment, or decrease inventory twice.
  The timeout job prevents abandoned PENDING_PAYMENT orders
  from holding stock indefinitely.
end note

@enduml
